# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# Each project also carries its own .gitignore. This file is the backstop for
# the things that are easy to leak from the repository root, and for the two
# categories the per-project files were found to miss: timestamped .env backups
# and packaged build artifacts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets.
#
# The allow-listed *.example files are the documentation of what has to be set;
# everything else that looks like an environment file stays out.
#
# `.env.bak-*` is called out because it is what actually bit: the per-project
# ignores list `.env`, `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`, none of which match a
# file named `.env.bak-2026-07-27T07-50-55-182Z`. Two of those existed, each
# holding a live MongoDB URI with credentials, both JWT signing secrets, the
# seed admin password and the website revalidation secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.env.bak-*
.env.bak-*
bundle.env
!bundle.env.example

# Keys and certificates, in case one is ever dropped in a working tree
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Packaged release artifacts.
#
# `Portal/dist-portal/` is 124 MB across 12,354 files and `dist-portal.zip` is
# 51 MB — over GitHub's 50 MB per-file warning and reproducible from source with
# `npm run build:bundle`. Neither belongs in history, where it cannot be removed
# without a rewrite.
dist-portal/
dist-portal.zip
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flutter / Dart — stmarks_portal_app
#
# The app carries its own .gitignore, but this is the backstop for the one that
# matters most: `.dart_tool/` is **419 MB** in this working tree, and `build/`
# is larger again. Both are regenerated by `flutter pub get` and `flutter build`
# and neither can be removed from history without a rewrite.
#
# `build/` is already matched by the generic rule above; it is restated here so
# that the reason it must never be committed is written next to the others.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/
*.iml
*.iws
.metadata

# Android
.gradle/
local.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
captures/

# iOS / macOS
Pods/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
**/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
**/ios/Flutter/App.framework
**/ios/Flutter/flutter_assets/

# Golden-file test output. The masters belong in the repository; the diffs and
# actual images written on a failing run do not.
test/failures/
**/test/failures/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data.
#
# **Media is deliberately NOT ignored.** An `uploads/` rule was added here and
# taken straight back out: it matched 337 real files — the church's images,
# thumbnails and videos in `Portal/backend/uploads/` — and it also swallowed
# `Portal-Docker/snapshot/`'s shipped media, because a negation cannot re-include
# anything inside an already-ignored directory. Photographs of this congregation
# are among the hardest things on the project to replace; they stay in the
# repository.
#
# What is left here is the database and its dumps, which are reproducible and
# which no one photographs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/db/
mongodb-data/
*.bson
*.mongodump/
dump/

# Portal backup archives. Each one contains every collection — password hashes
# and the contact inbox included — so a stray archive in a working tree is the
# whole installation in one file.
backups/
*.csistmc-backup
*-backup-*.json

# Test and coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*



# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

# Local tooling
.eslintcache
.turbo/
.vercel
.cache/
*.tmp
tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated documents.
#
# `docs/*.docx` is built from the matching Markdown by a script — the Markdown
# is the source of truth, and committing both invites the two to drift with no
# way to tell which was edited last. Send the Word file; keep the Markdown.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `**/docs/` and not `docs/`: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory holding this file, so `docs/*.docx` would only ever have matched a
# `/docs/` at the repository root — and every docs folder here is one level
# down, in `WebsiteRT/` or `Portal/`.
**/docs/*.docx
~$*.docx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody adds them later by reflex:
#
#   pubspec.lock          an application pins its dependencies; only a *package*
#                         leaves this out
#   package-lock.json     same reason
#   snapshot/             Portal-Docker's shipped first-boot content
#   public/frames/        the home page's cinematic sequence — 300 real assets,
#                         not build output
#   *.example             the documentation of every secret that must be set
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
